    "qualityRules": [
      "Customer behavior knowledge explains patterned actions and contexts that shape attention, evaluation, purchase, and loyalty.",
      "Buying motivation covers the drivers—jobs-to-be-done, status, fear reduction, belonging—that make offers relevant.",
      "Emotional triggers are affective cues (relief, pride, fear of loss, joy) that intensify engagement when matched to brand and truth.",
      "Trust building reduces perceived risk via proof, transparency, consistency, and credible messengers.",
      "Decision-making psychology covers heuristics, evaluation criteria, and friction that shape yes/no/wait outcomes.",
      "Attention psychology explains salience, novelty, pattern interrupt, and cognitive limits that govern whether creative is noticed and retained.",
      "Product perception is the constructed sense of quality, efficacy, and desirability formed from visuals, demos, context, and claims.",
      "Consumer expectations are anticipated standards for quality, speed, claims, and creative norms that shape satisfaction and trust.",
      "Customer satisfaction is the gap between expected and experienced outcomes; creative should set honest expectations and reinforce success.",
      "Customer retention strategies increase repeat purchase and advocacy through value reinforcement, habit, community, and service."
    ],
